From c1f0a2ce11df1e41f63cc032cd5a69af7e8ff6ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Kulke <magnuskulke@linux.microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:24:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] target/i386/mshv: add soft-mmu for pagewalk

RH-Author: Paolo Bonzini <pbonzini@redhat.com>
RH-MergeRequest: 580: target/i386/mshv: add soft-mmu for pagewalk
RH-Jira: RHEL-283121
RH-Acked-by: Richard W.M. Jones <rjones@redhat.com>
RH-Acked-by: Maxim Levitsky <None>
RH-Commit: [2/2] 732145b446896e06cb6132984e50874accfc100f

To work around problems with HVCALL_TRANSLATE_VIRTUAL_ADDRESS that is used
in MMIO emulation we introduce a software mmu implementation for mshv that we
use to perform a table walk in userland. This attempts to mimic the
semantics and behaviour of the hvcall. The table walk implementation has
limitations, which are bubbled up in userland as UNSUPPORTED errors.

The supplied unit test suite documents those limitations.

Downstream only patch, corresponding to upstream x86_mmu.c
and commits 1c85a4a3d7 and cb02fc2284.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Kulke <magnuskulke@linux.microsoft.com>
